-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 7: SERVICE IN SINGAPORE.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE: the text says yes on these facts.  JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words
-- (a flat negative, an "unless", an "if", "where" or "when" that is not met, "only if", a stated period that has run).
-- NOTHING: the text does not answer (a list not closed, a grant limited by its own wording, a scope limit with no "only",
-- a term or law outside the sources).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§§ `Order 7, Rule 1 -- methods of service generally`

-- Rule 1(1)(a): personal service is open where one of three things is so.  "where" not met: JUST FALSE.
-- src:572 | personal service, where expressly required by these Rules or any written law, or where the Court orders such service, or where the serving party
-- src:572 | decides to do so voluntarily; or
@ref O 7 r 1(1)(a) (src:572)
GIVEN `personal service is expressly required by these Rules or any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court orders personal service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the serving party decides to serve personally voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 1(1)(a) a document may be served by personal service` MEANS
    IF `personal service is expressly required by these Rules or any written law` OR `the Court orders personal service` OR `the serving party decides to serve personally voluntarily`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "personal service, where expressly required by these Rules or any written law, or where the Court orders such service, or where the serving party decides to do so voluntarily"

-- src:574 | ordinary service.
@ref O 7 r 1(1)(b) (src:574)
GIVEN `the document is required to be served under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 1(1)(b) a document may be served by ordinary service` MEANS
    IF `the document is required to be served under these Rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches "Any document that is required to be served under these Rules"

-- src:575 | (2) The Court may, in an appropriate case, dispense with personal service or with ordinary service or with service altogether.
@ref O 7 r 1(2) (src:575)
GIVEN `it is an appropriate case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 1(2) the Court may dispense with personal service, ordinary service or service altogether` MEANS
    IF `it is an appropriate case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in an appropriate case"

§§ `Order 7, Rule 2 -- personal service`

DECLARE `o 7 r 2(1) the manner of personal service` IS ONE OF
    `o 7 r 2(1)(a) a copy left with the natural person`
    `o 7 r 2(1)(a) a copy left with the agent of an overseas principal under Rule 4`
    `o 7 r 2(1)(b) a copy left with the chairperson or president of the entity`
    `o 7 r 2(1)(b) a copy left with the secretary, treasurer or other officer of the entity`
    `o 7 r 2(1)(c) according to the requirements of a written law`
    `o 7 r 2(1)(d) in a manner agreed with the person or entity to be served`
    `o 7 r 2(1) some other manner`

-- src:577-584 | 2. —(1) Personal service of a document is effected — ( a ) on a natural person by leaving a copy of the document with that person, or the person’s
-- src:577-584 | agent if that person is an overseas principal under Rule 4; ( b ) on any entity by leaving a copy of the document with the chairperson or president of
-- src:577-584 | the entity, or the secretary, treasurer or other officer; ( c ) on any person or entity according to the requirements of any written law; or ( d ) in
-- src:577-584 | any manner agreed with the person or the entity to be served.
@ref O 7 r 2(1) (src:577-584)
GIVEN person IS A `Kind of person`
      manner IS A `o 7 r 2(1) the manner of personal service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 2(1) personal service is effected` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `o 7 r 2(1)(a) a copy left with the natural person` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (a) is "on a natural person"; the entity limbs are (b), (c) and (d)
    WHEN `o 7 r 2(1)(a) a copy left with the agent of an overseas principal under Rule 4` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (a) is "on a natural person"
    WHEN `o 7 r 2(1)(b) a copy left with the chairperson or president of the entity` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (b) is "on any entity"
    WHEN `o 7 r 2(1)(b) a copy left with the secretary, treasurer or other officer of the entity` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (b) is "on any entity"
    WHEN `o 7 r 2(1)(c) according to the requirements of a written law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 7 r 2(1)(d) in a manner agreed with the person or entity to be served` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 7 r 2(1) some other manner` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the Rule says how personal service "is effected" and has no "only"

DECLARE `o 7 r 2(2) who serves` IS ONE OF
    `o 7 r 2(2)(a) a process server of the Court`
    `o 7 r 2(2)(b) a solicitor`
    `o 7 r 2(2)(c) a solicitor's employee`
    `o 7 r 2(2)(d) a litigant who is not legally represented`
    `o 7 r 2(2)(d) an employee of a litigant who is not legally represented`
    `o 7 r 2(2)(e) another person whom the Registrar has allowed in the particular case or generally`
    `o 7 r 2(2) any other person`

-- src:585-594 | (2) The following persons may effect personal service: ( a ) a process server of the Court; ( b ) a solicitor; ( c ) a solicitor’s employee; ( d ) a
-- src:585-594 | litigant who is not legally represented or such a person’s employee; ( e ) any other person that the Registrar may allow in a particular case or
-- src:585-594 | generally.
@ref O 7 r 2(2) (src:585-594)
GIVEN server IS A `o 7 r 2(2) who serves`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 2(2) the person may effect personal service` MEANS
    CONSIDER server
    WHEN `o 7 r 2(2) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following persons may effect personal service" names who may and does not say who may not
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:595 | (3) If the process server of the Court effects service, the Registrar must notify the requesting person of the fact and manner of such service.
@ref O 7 r 2(3) (src:595)
GIVEN `the process server of the Court effected the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 2(3) the Registrar must notify the requesting person of the fact and manner of service` MEANS
    IF `the process server of the Court effected the service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the process server of the Court effects service"

§§ `Order 7, Rule 3 -- ordinary service`

DECLARE `o 7 r 3 the manner of ordinary service` IS ONE OF
    `o 7 r 3(a)(i) leaving it at or posting it to the natural person's usual or last known address`
    `o 7 r 3(a)(i) leaving it at or posting it to the business address of the natural person's solicitor`
    `o 7 r 3(a)(ii) leaving it at or posting it to the entity's registered or principal office`
    `o 7 r 3(a)(ii) leaving it at or posting it to the entity's last known place of business`
    `o 7 r 3(a)(ii) leaving it at or posting it to the entity's solicitor's address`
    `o 7 r 3(b) electronic mail at the address provided by the party to be served`
    `o 7 r 3(c) fax`
    `o 7 r 3(d) a manner agreed between the parties`
    `o 7 r 3(e) a manner the Court may direct`
    `o 7 r 3(f) a manner provided under a written law`
    `o 7 r 3 some other manner`

-- Two inputs that only some limbs read: for (a)(ii) "if none exists" and for (c) "only if".
-- src:597-614 | 3. Ordinary service of a document may be effected — ( a ) by leaving the document at or posting it to — (i) in the case of a natural person, the
-- src:597-614 | person’s usual or last known address or the business address of the person’s solicitor; or (ii) in the case of an entity, its registered or principal
-- src:597-614 | office or, if none exists, its last known place of business or its solicitor’s address; ( b ) by electronic mail at the electronic mail address
-- src:597-614 | provided by the party to be served; ( c ) by fax, but only if — (i) both the serving party and the party to be served act by solicitor; and (ii) the
-- src:597-614 | solicitor acting for the party to be served indicates to the solicitor acting for the serving party that the firstmentioned solicitor is willing to
-- src:597-614 | accept service at a specified fax number and the document is transmitted to that number; ( d ) in any manner agreed between the parties; ( e ) in any
-- src:597-614 | manner which the Court may direct, including the use of electronic means; or ( f ) in any manner provided under any written law.
@ref O 7 r 3 (src:597-614)
GIVEN person IS A `Kind of person`
      manner IS A `o 7 r 3 the manner of ordinary service`
      `the entity has a registered or principal office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both the serving party and the party to be served act by solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the solicitor for the party to be served indicated willingness to accept service at a specified fax number and the document is transmitted to that number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 3 ordinary service may be effected in that manner` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(a)(i) leaving it at or posting it to the natural person's usual or last known address` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (a)(i) is "in the case of a natural person"
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(a)(i) leaving it at or posting it to the business address of the natural person's solicitor` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (a)(i) is "in the case of a natural person"
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(a)(ii) leaving it at or posting it to the entity's registered or principal office` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (a)(ii) is "in the case of an entity"
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(a)(ii) leaving it at or posting it to the entity's last known place of business` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN
            IF `the entity has a registered or principal office`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "its registered or principal office or, if none exists, its last known place of business"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (a)(ii) is "in the case of an entity"
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(a)(ii) leaving it at or posting it to the entity's solicitor's address` THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN Entity incorporated THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Natural person` age THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): limb (a)(ii) is "in the case of an entity"
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(b) electronic mail at the address provided by the party to be served` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(c) fax` THEN
        IF `both the serving party and the party to be served act by solicitor` AND `the solicitor for the party to be served indicated willingness to accept service at a specified fax number and the document is transmitted to that number`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by fax, but only if (i) both the serving party and the party to be served act by solicitor; and (ii) the solicitor acting for the party to be served indicates ... and the document is transmitted to that number"
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(d) a manner agreed between the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(e) a manner the Court may direct` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 7 r 3(f) a manner provided under a written law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 7 r 3 some other manner` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the Rule says ordinary service "may be effected" in the listed ways and has no "only"

§§ `Order 7, Rule 4 -- service on the agent of an overseas principal`

-- src:616-621 | 4. —(1) The Court may, on a summons without notice, direct service to be effected on an agent or manager of a principal, if it is satisfied that — ( a
-- src:616-621 | ) an action, including the administration of an estate, is against a principal who does not reside within or is absent from Singapore; ( b ) the agent
-- src:616-621 | or manager has personal control or management within Singapore over the principal’s affairs that specifically relate to the action at the time of
-- src:616-621 | service; and ( c ) either the authority of the agent or manager has not been terminated, or the agent or manager has an ongoing business relationship
-- src:616-621 | with the principal at the time of the application.
@ref O 7 r 4(1) (src:616-621)
GIVEN `the action is against a principal who does not reside within or is absent from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent or manager has personal control or management within Singapore over the principal's affairs that specifically relate to the action at the time of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority of the agent or manager has not been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent or manager has an ongoing business relationship with the principal at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 4(1) the Court may direct service on an agent or manager of a principal` MEANS
    IF `the action is against a principal who does not reside within or is absent from Singapore`
       AND `the agent or manager has personal control or management within Singapore over the principal's affairs that specifically relate to the action at the time of service`
       AND (`the authority of the agent or manager has not been terminated` OR `the agent or manager has an ongoing business relationship with the principal at the time of the application`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is satisfied that (a) ... (b) ...; and (c) either the authority of the agent or manager has not been terminated, or the agent or manager has an ongoing business relationship"

-- src:622 | (2) An agent of a ship is deemed to be the agent of the owner or of the charterer of the ship under this Rule.
@ref O 7 r 4(2) (src:622)
GIVEN `the person is an agent of a ship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 4(2) the person is deemed the agent of the owner or of the charterer of the ship` MEANS
    IF `the person is an agent of a ship`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is for "An agent of a ship"

-- The duty itself, as a yes/no beside the timed function below (the duty is also traced in `roc1-duties.l4`): it exists if the claimant knows the principal's overseas address.
-- src:623 | (3) The claimant must send a copy of the order of Court authorising service under this Rule and of the relevant document to be served to the
-- src:623 | principal’s overseas address by prepaid registered post, if the claimant knows that address, within 14 days after service on the agent or manager.
@ref O 7 r 4(3) (src:623)
GIVEN `the claimant knows the principal's overseas address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 4(3) the claimant must send a copy of the order and of the document to the principal's overseas address` MEANS
    IF `the claimant knows the principal's overseas address`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the claimant knows that address" (an "if" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:623 | (3) The claimant must send a copy of the order of Court authorising service under this Rule and of the relevant document to be served to the
-- src:623 | principal’s overseas address by prepaid registered post, if the claimant knows that address, within 14 days after service on the agent or manager.
@ref O 7 r 4(3) (src:623)
`o 7 r 4(3) the period for sending the copy to the principal` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:623 | (3) The claimant must send a copy of the order of Court authorising service under this Rule and of the relevant document to be served to the
-- src:623 | principal’s overseas address by prepaid registered post, if the claimant knows that address, within 14 days after service on the agent or manager.
@ref O 7 r 4(3) (src:623)
GIVEN `the claimant knows the principal's overseas address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the order and of the document is sent to that address by prepaid registered post` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of service on the agent or manager` IS A DATE
      `the date the copy is sent` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 4(3) the claimant has sent the copy to the principal as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claimant knows the principal's overseas address`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the claimant knows that address"
        IF NOT `the copy of the order and of the document is sent to that address by prepaid registered post`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must send a copy ... to the principal’s overseas address by prepaid registered post"
        OTHERWISE `o 3 r 3 the act is in time` `o 7 r 4(3) the period for sending the copy to the principal` `the date of service on the agent or manager` `the date the copy is sent` calendar `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`

§§ `Order 7, Rule 5 -- service in certain actions for possession of immovable property`

