      `no person appears to be in possession of the immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `service cannot otherwise be effected on any party to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 5 the Court may authorise service by placing the document on a conspicuous part of the property` MEANS
    IF `there is a claim for possession of immovable property` AND `no person appears to be in possession of the immovable property` AND `service cannot otherwise be effected on any party to be served`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a claim for possession of immovable property ... if the Court is satisfied that (a) no person appears to be in possession of the immovable property; and (b) service cannot otherwise be effected"

§§ `Order 7, Rule 6 -- service on a Minister, department or the Attorney-General`

-- The effect of section 20 of the Government Proceedings Act and of Order 59, Rule 3 is not in this part's range or sources:
-- the Rule says they "apply", and that is the answer given here.
-- src:630 | 6. Where for the purpose of or in connection with any proceedings, not being civil proceedings by or against the Government within the meaning of Part
-- src:630 | III of the Government Proceedings Act, any document is required by any written law or these Rules to be served on the Minister of a Government
-- src:630 | department which is an authorised department for the purposes of that Act, or on such a department or on the Attorney‑General, section 20 of that Act
-- src:630 | and Order 59, Rule 3 apply in relation to the service of the document as they apply in relation to the service of documents required to be served on
-- src:630 | the Government for the purpose of or in connection with any civil proceedings by or against the Government.
@ref O 7 r 6 (src:630)
GIVEN `the proceedings are civil proceedings by or against the Government within the meaning of Part III of the Government Proceedings Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is required by written law or these Rules to be served on the Minister of an authorised department, or on such a department, or on the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 6 section 20 of the Government Proceedings Act and Order 59, Rule 3 apply to the service` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the proceedings are civil proceedings by or against the Government within the meaning of Part III of the Government Proceedings Act`) AND `the document is required by written law or these Rules to be served on the Minister of an authorised department, or on such a department, or on the Attorney-General`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... not being civil proceedings by or against the Government ... any document is required ... to be served on the Minister ..., or on such a department or on the Attorney‑General"

