§§ `Order 7, Rule 8 -- time for service (seam S-S1)`

-- Before 5 p.m. the service is deemed effected that day; after 5 p.m., the following day (the Rule says "the following day", not the next court day).
-- At exactly 5 p.m. the Rule says neither: the DATE answer is NOTHING (a date cannot carry JUST FALSE); the yes/no twin `o 7 r 8 this Rule deems the day of service` answers JUST FALSE, "when" counting as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)).  (roc-core's note says "no gap"; the text has one.)
-- Subject to any written law and these Rules including Order 28: service through the electronic filing service is Order 28's, so NOTHING here.
-- src:635 | 8. —(1) Subject to any written law and these Rules (including Order 28 regulating the electronic filing service), when service is effected before 5
-- src:635 | p.m. on any particular day, service is deemed to have been effected on that day. (2) When service is effected after 5 p.m. on any particular day,
-- src:635 | service is deemed to have been effected on the following day.
@ref O 7 r 8 (src:635)
GIVEN event IS A `Service event`
      `a written law or another Rule provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a written law or another Rule provides otherwise` OR event's `service method` EQUALS `Service through the electronic filing service`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any written law and these Rules (including Order 28 regulating the electronic filing service)"
        IF event's `service moment`'s `minutes after midnight` LESS THAN 1020
            THEN JUST (event's `service moment`'s `day of the moment`)
        IF event's `service moment`'s `minutes after midnight` GREATER THAN 1020
            THEN JUST (event's `service moment`'s `day of the moment` PLUS 1)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): service at exactly 5 p.m. is neither "before 5 p.m." nor "after 5 p.m."

-- src:635 | 8. —(1) Subject to any written law and these Rules (including Order 28 regulating the electronic filing service), when service is effected before 5
-- src:635 | p.m. on any particular day, service is deemed to have been effected on that day. (2) When service is effected after 5 p.m. on any particular day,
-- src:635 | service is deemed to have been effected on the following day.
@ref O 7 r 8 (src:635)
GIVEN event IS A `Service event`
      `a written law or another Rule provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 7 r 8 this Rule deems the day of service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a written law or another Rule provides otherwise` OR event's `service method` EQUALS `Service through the electronic filing service`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any written law and these Rules (including Order 28 regulating the electronic filing service)"
        IF event's `service moment`'s `minutes after midnight` EQUALS 1020
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when service is effected before 5 p.m." and "When service is effected after 5 p.m." are both unmet at exactly 5 p.m. ("when" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c); the date function stays NOTHING because a date cannot say no)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
